- Single merged Mesh (wing arch 16 segs, 2 emissive edge strips via canvas 2x1 emissiveMap, torso, head, 14 lines). Placement: rotation.set(-bank, yaw, 0, 'YXZ').
- Test: npm run typecheck OK; npm run build OK; npm run test:explore: all pass (1a-1h, 2a-2g, console clean). Glider adds +2 draw calls day and night.
- TDD note: implementation was written before the test run (hook needed the code), so a clean RED run was not captured. First GREEN attempt had 3 test bugs (info.autoReset=false in app so calls accumulate; uNight needs frames after setNight) - fixed in test only.
- Screenshots seen: takeoff-ngay: glider from behind, orange wing arch, lines converging on pilot at bottom edge, Han river/city ahead. takeoff-dem: same, white glowing edges on wing; the first version only lit the leading edge (invisible from behind), so I added the trailing edge strip.
- Concerns: HANG (0.45*span), CHORD, ARCH are local constants in glider.ts, not CONFIG; `lines` is used as lines-per-side count (config comment), not hang distance.

